$80:F950                       # the same shape, testing player_weapon 4 and using
                               # $0040 -- no caller anywhere in the cartridge
# $80:E86D and $80:F935 run on the **player thread's** direct page, so $0E, $1E,
# $2A, $30, $32, $50, $52 and $70 there are thread locals. Do not read them
# against the absolute names below -- see port/floor.h.
# There was a `$80:AE00 tile_walkable` here for a long time and it was never a
# routine: $AE00 is the second byte of `$80:ADFF JSL $80AD1C`, it is an opcode
# boundary in no execution, and the profile counts it zero times in ten movies.
# The thing it described is `$80:AE14`, four instructions past the end of the
# routine it pointed into. Symbols read off a listing want the same treatment
# as the listing itself -- see the `.db` table in docs/analysis-tools.md.

